WEBVTT

00:00.450 --> 00:03.212
This is Part 3: measure and quote.

00:03.162 --> 00:06.669
Good numbers make a good quote, and a good plan for the crew.

00:07.634 --> 00:09.667
There are two ways to measure.

00:09.617 --> 00:12.753
Use the measuring wheel only when the roofline is flat.

00:12.753 --> 00:15.554
Roll it on the ground, right under the eave.

00:15.554 --> 00:21.955
For everything else, like peaks, slopes, dormers, and soffit on top of a roof, count the soffit pieces.

00:22.906 --> 00:24.800
Here's the soffit math.

00:24.750 --> 00:27.065
Four inch soffit is the most common.

00:27.065 --> 00:29.681
Count divided by three equals feet.

00:29.681 --> 00:31.810
Six inch soffit is rare.

00:31.810 --> 00:33.801
Count divided by two.

00:33.801 --> 00:37.713
Eight inch soffit: count times eight, divided by twelve.

00:38.682 --> 00:40.391
Measure in this order.

00:40.341 --> 00:42.910
Ask the client where the lights should start.

00:42.910 --> 00:47.517
If they don't care, start at a downspout on one side, and go left to right.

00:47.517 --> 00:51.915
Do the bottoms with the wheel first: left bottom, front bottom, right bottom.

00:51.915 --> 00:55.584
Then the tops: right top, front top, left top.

00:56.546 --> 00:58.289
Then add the peaks.

00:58.239 --> 01:00.253
Look at the number on your wheel.

01:00.253 --> 01:02.290
Say it reads eighty feet.

01:02.290 --> 01:05.230
Count the soffit on the peak and do the soffit math.

01:05.230 --> 01:06.908
That's the peak feet.

01:06.908 --> 01:11.388
On your phone, add the peak feet to the wheel number, then roll the wheel up to that total.

01:11.388 --> 01:14.570
Now you have one running number, in one place.

01:15.538 --> 01:17.270
Quoting an add-on?

01:17.220 --> 01:20.414
Measure everything except the add-on and write it down.

01:20.414 --> 01:22.938
Then measure the add-on by itself.

01:22.938 --> 01:25.333
Each one is its own line in the quote.

01:26.298 --> 01:29.754
Take the photos right after you measure, with your phone camera.

01:29.704 --> 01:32.598
One from the front left, one from the front right.

01:32.598 --> 01:34.901
Every part you measured must show.

01:34.901 --> 01:38.478
Then mark them up in the markup app, always in this colour order.

01:38.478 --> 01:41.325
Red is option one, the base or front.

01:41.325 --> 01:43.906
Blue is option two, like the back.

01:43.906 --> 01:46.591
Then yellow, green and purple.

01:46.591 --> 01:50.572
Draw the bottom first, left to right, then the top, then the peaks.

01:51.530 --> 01:54.072
Mark the injections on the photo too.

01:54.022 --> 01:59.323
Draw a dot every fifty lights, about thirty-three feet, and write the light count between the dots.

01:59.323 --> 02:01.348
Never over fifty-six.

02:01.348 --> 02:05.770
Mark every roofline, the total feet for each run, and where the box goes.

02:05.770 --> 02:08.663
The crew should never have to work this out on a ladder.

02:09.610 --> 02:11.597
How does the signal travel?

02:11.547 --> 02:13.109
Think of a river.

02:13.109 --> 02:14.822
The box is the lake.

02:14.822 --> 02:17.982
The signal starts at the box and flows left to right.

02:17.982 --> 02:20.725
The bottom and the top each need their own path.

02:20.725 --> 02:22.889
It can jump up at a downspout.

02:22.889 --> 02:26.130
And a Y-split is where the river forks, like at a peak.

02:27.090 --> 02:28.903
A few words to know.

02:28.853 --> 02:33.714
Channels, or zones, are up to four parts of the house the client can control on their own.

02:33.714 --> 02:35.658
One channel is best.

02:35.658 --> 02:37.302
It's the easiest.

02:37.302 --> 02:40.983
Injection is a wire that feeds new power every fifty lights.

02:40.983 --> 02:42.684
It's on every job.

02:42.684 --> 02:44.408
And hide the wire.

02:44.408 --> 02:51.087
Put open wire in cable sleeve, and tuck it behind trim, corner pieces, siding lines, or inside the track.

02:52.034 --> 02:53.419
Which track?

02:53.369 --> 02:55.313
Ask these questions.

02:55.313 --> 02:57.697
Normal soffit with a fascia lip?

02:57.697 --> 02:59.329
Use hat track.

02:59.329 --> 03:03.172
If not, is there four inches or more of flat wall at the roofline?

03:03.172 --> 03:04.792
Use backtrack.

03:04.792 --> 03:09.433
And if a gutter covers that flat wall, use gutter track, with the lights pointing down.

03:09.433 --> 03:10.938
None of these?

03:10.938 --> 03:13.114
Call your lead before you quote.

03:13.114 --> 03:16.471
Never put track on vinyl siding, and never use glue.

03:16.471 --> 03:19.133
All track is screwed on and colour-matched.

03:20.098 --> 03:21.888
How many boxes?

03:21.838 --> 03:26.213
Front only: one box, if it's a hundred sixty-five feet or less.

03:26.213 --> 03:29.396
Front and back with no sides: at least two.

03:29.396 --> 03:32.266
We can't run signal down the side of a house.

03:32.266 --> 03:34.882
A full house: use the quick table.

03:34.882 --> 03:36.930
Most need two or more.

03:36.930 --> 03:38.898
This is a big change.

03:38.898 --> 03:42.335
The old manual said one box does four hundred feet.

03:42.335 --> 03:44.743
Now it's about a hundred sixty-five.

03:45.690 --> 03:47.538
Where does the box go?

03:47.488 --> 03:51.677
The golden rule: where the lights start, close to a GFCI plug.

03:51.677 --> 03:54.687
Vinyl siding with a soffit plug near the start?

03:54.687 --> 03:57.627
Mount the box right under it with four screws.

03:57.627 --> 03:59.039
Best job.

03:59.039 --> 04:01.018
Plug far from the start?

04:01.018 --> 04:04.988
Call your lead about getting power there, or do an in-garage install.

04:04.988 --> 04:11.353
On a stucco house, the first choice is the back fascia board, then in the garage, and last, on the stucco.

04:11.353 --> 04:15.057
The old manual said to hide an extension cord under the siding.

04:15.057 --> 04:17.488
Don't, until you've asked your lead.

04:18.434 --> 04:22.191
Every quote goes through the quoting app, the same way every time.

04:22.141 --> 04:26.887
Make the client, with first and last name, phone, email and address.

04:26.887 --> 04:29.259
Create the quote from the lights template.

04:29.259 --> 04:31.482
The quantity is the feet you measured.

04:31.482 --> 04:34.259
Add a box line for each extra box.

04:34.259 --> 04:36.540
Attach every marked-up photo.

04:36.540 --> 04:41.921
And for each extra option, turn on both switches: set as option, and recommend line item.

04:41.921 --> 04:44.908
The front, or base, line doesn't get them.

04:44.908 --> 04:47.315
Miss one, and the total is wrong.

04:48.274 --> 04:49.508
Recap.

04:49.458 --> 04:52.826
The wheel on flat lines, soffit counts for the rest.

04:52.826 --> 04:55.118
Bottoms first, then tops.

04:55.118 --> 04:57.884
Two photos, marked up in colour order.

04:57.884 --> 05:00.014
A dot every fifty lights.

05:00.014 --> 05:02.653
Never track on vinyl, never glue.

05:02.653 --> 05:05.893
And one box covers about a hundred sixty-five feet.

05:06.858 --> 05:08.497
That's Part 3.

05:08.447 --> 05:11.433
Now take the Part 3 quiz in your training portal.
